Technitium DNS Server on FenrirOS
=================================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled and there is no data or
configuration.

    dinitctl enable technitium-dns

The server keeps its configuration and zones in /var/lib/technitium-dns. Its
web console is on http://<host>:5380/ ; on the first visit it asks you to set
the admin password (or set DNS_SERVER_ADMIN_PASSWORD before the first start).
Do this at once, on a trusted network. It runs as the technitium-dns user and
may bind port 53 and other ports below 1024; anything else on port 53
(dnsmasq, unbound, a resolver) must be stopped first. The built-in DHCP server
needs the network interface access you give it; DNS-over-QUIC and HTTP/3
need libmsquic, which is not packaged.

Apps (Advanced Blocking, query logs, Split Horizon, geo routing, ...) are
built from source and shipped as zip files in /usr/share/technitium-dns/apps:
install them from the web console (Apps > Install, choose the file). The
console's own app store downloads from technitium.com instead; use that only
if you want to.
